WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:06.473
[ Piano playing ]

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:08.841
-Hi, guys. This is Jimmy Fallon,

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:10.943
and this is "The Tonight Show:
Home Edition,"

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:12.144
I guess you can call it.

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:13.946
We really don't know
what this is.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:16.983
But I wanted to put something
out there for you guys

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:20.186
so that we can just have
some levity

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:24.357
in these bizarre times.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:29.362
What we're doing right now
is I'm in a room in my house.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.097
My camera operator is my wife.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.164
-Hi.
-Hi, honey.

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:33.399
Thank you for doing this.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.703
And we have my dog Gary.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.104
Gary.
[ Snaps fingers ]

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.972
My dog Gary is my first guess.

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:42.508
Hi, Gary. Sit. Sit.
Gary, sit.

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.144
Good girl.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.878
-Daddy?
-And then, yeah, hi, Franny.

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:48.848
And just gonna happen.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.517
Franny, do you want
to play the drums?

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:53.252
-No.
-Okay. Perfect.

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:56.923
Well, it is -- We're gonna
just say hi to everyone,

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.525
and I hope everyone's safe.

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:02.294
I want to wish everyone
a happy St. Patrick's Day.

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:04.230
Today is St. Paddy's Day,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.298
so happy St. Patrick's Day
to everyone.

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:07.967
-Da-da?
-Yeah.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.436
-I wanna play
"The Incredibles" game.

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:11.804
-I know. I know.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.073
-Let me just do this,
and then we'll play, okay?

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.408
-Uh-huh.
-Thank you.

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:17.643
Can you draw me a drawing?

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:19.044
-No.
-Thank you.

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:20.813
-No.
-I heard you.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:24.250
I asked my other daughter to --
-Gary, come on!

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.085
Wha!

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:30.223
-Uh, to draw me a shamrock,
and this is...

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:33.659
-Want to play with me?
-Please -- Thank you.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:35.528
This is the shamrock
she drew me.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.930
It's a green poop emoji.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.233
So we're gonna be doing
some jokes for you,

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.634
maybe a song, or just something.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.070
We'll switch it up every night,
but we want to give you

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.606
some type of content
every single night

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.242
for as long
as we're gonna do this.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:52.678
Every night, we're gonna do
a different charity

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.548
and talk about
what they're doing for people.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:02:00.052
Tonight's charity is...

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.821
feedingamerica.org.

00:02:02.821 --> 00:02:08.861
Feeding America has
200 food banks nationwide.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:12.198
They do so much for everyone
who needs food,

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.432
and especially at this time,

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:16.902
I always think of people
who are out of work now

00:02:16.902 --> 00:02:20.640
to everyone's staying in
who can't get food.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.909
There's also --
I think of a child out there

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:27.313
who just relies
on one meal a day,

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.981
and they can't even get that.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.750
These people work tirelessly
to make sure when that happens,

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.519
these people get fed.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:37.857
So please donate whatever
you can to feedingamerica.org,

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:42.295
whether it be $1, $5,
anything is fantastic.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.830
All of the drawing tonight
and the graphics

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:48.367
and artwork are from my --
It's from my 6-year-old.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.870
So this is Winnie's.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.706
Just so you know, that's
my graphics department here.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.109
All right. I'm gonna do some
jokes for you guys right now.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.478
And I want to thank
all the writers

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.312
who are sending jokes
in from home.

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:04.517
I appreciate it, and it was
last minute, but thank you.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.985
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.754
I'm so excited to be doing
the show from my panic room --

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:11.857
I mean, living room.

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:16.795
[ Nancy and Jimmy laugh ]

00:03:16.795 --> 00:03:19.698
Guys, I'm gonna do some
monologue jokes here, okay?

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:22.034
So, uh, I'm gonna read them
to you here.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.035
Of course,
there's no audience --

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:25.104
Well, there is an audience,
my wife,

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.372
but she doesn't really laugh
at everything

00:03:27.372 --> 00:03:28.874
that I say, so we'll see.

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:32.979
But if things are funny, but,
hey, just take it with grain --

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:35.081
You know, come on. You know what
we're trying to do here.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.749
Here we go.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.217
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.653
I'm so excited to be doing
the show from my panic room --

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.789
I mean, living room.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:45.357
As you can see,
I'm doing the show from my home

00:03:45.357 --> 00:03:47.259
for two reasons --
First, to stop the spread

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:48.528
of the coronavirus.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:51.964
Second, so I can write off
my real-estate taxes.

00:03:51.964 --> 00:03:54.100
That's right, I'm doing the show
from my house in New York,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.669
and this is how crazy
New York traffic is.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:57.903
I'm doing the show
from my living room,

00:03:57.903 --> 00:04:00.639
and I was still
20 minutes late getting in.

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:02.107
But I hope you guys are like me

00:04:02.107 --> 00:04:04.076
and enjoying all this
extra time with your family.

00:04:04.076 --> 00:04:05.244
Isn't it great?

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:07.446
Today, we binge watched
a couple TV shows,

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.048
then we checked out
a couple movies,

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.249
and then finally,
my kids said to me,

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:13.152
"Dad, can we watch
something we like?"

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.620
So far, it's been pretty fun
at the house.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.155
We've been doing lots of
coloring,

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.391
making pillow forts,
doing arts and crafts,

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:21.794
while the kids have been
watching TV in the basement.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.429
But with classes canceled
around the country,

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:25.264
lots of people
are homeschooling their kids.

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:27.400
I'm homeschooling my kids, and
it's working out pretty well.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.035
In fact, my kids have already
learned a valuable lesson --

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:31.871
Their dad is an idiot.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:33.739
Seriously, after about
15 minutes, my kids said,

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.508
"We're transferring
to mom's class."

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.842
-[ Chuckles ]

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:38.911
-You liked that one?

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.446
But it's been an interesting
few days.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.981
I never thought putting on pants

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.849
would feel like
an accomplishment.

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:45.083
These are crazy times.

00:04:45.083 --> 00:04:47.119
We're being told not to visit
senior citizens

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:49.922
and to FaceTime them instead.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.057
Whoever came up with that idea
clearly hasn't tried to

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:55.294
FaceTime with someone over 70.
It's like, "No, hold it --

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:57.997
No, hold the phone away --
Okay.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.832
All right, now --
He turned it off.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:02.668
Turn it -- Let's call him back."

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:07.540
I want to wish everyone
a happy St. Patrick's Day.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:12.511
Oh, no, that joke,
we aren't gonna do.

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:17.250
We're not gonna do that joke,
'cause it's in the song.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.851
Some big sports news today.

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.319
Tom Brady announced that he
is leaving

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:23.790
the New England Patriots
on St. Patrick's Day.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:28.094
Yikes. For Boston, that's like
getting dumped on your birthday.

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.128
At least Brady's announcement

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:30.496
gave ESPN something
to talk about.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:31.964
Yesterday on "SportsCenter,"

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:36.369
they were airing the NBA's
best bounce passes of 2009.

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:37.770
That's our monologue,
everybody.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.139
Whoo!
-Whoo!

00:05:41.139 --> 00:05:43.509
-On St. --
-Winnie!

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:46.879
-Oh.
-Mom!

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:50.649
Dad! Mom!
-Okay.

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:52.117
-On St. Patrick's Day --

00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:56.422
That should be a shamrock --
we have to have the staples.

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.590
Of course,
I know in these times,

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.860
we can't go out,
but we can celebrate.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:05.398 line:0%
Of course, Guinness
is the beer of choice,

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.933 line:0%
the stout from Ireland.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:12.137 line:0%
And the way
a Guinness works is...

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:15.707 line:0%
you pour it --
Smoother than that, hopefully.

00:06:15.707 --> 00:06:18.377 line:0%
[ Nancy and Jimmy chuckling ]
That sounded so gross.

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:22.247 line:0%
I feel like it just exploded
from the inside out.

00:06:22.247 --> 00:06:23.416 line:0%
All right, so, look.

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:24.683 line:0%
So it looks like --
You go, what is this?

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:26.018 line:0%
This is a cloudy mess.

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:29.621 line:0%
Almost looks like -- But see it
all falling right there?

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:31.557 line:0%
How beautiful is that?

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:34.359 line:0%
That right there -- That will
all eventually clear up,

00:06:34.359 --> 00:06:38.397 line:0%
and it'll be dark, black,
with a nice white head on top.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:39.698 line:0%
It looks really good.

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:41.200 line:0%
Of course, you have soda bread.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.101 line:0%
This is an Irish staple.

00:06:43.101 --> 00:06:46.838
Not many people --
If you bake this at home,

00:06:46.838 --> 00:06:48.474
people in the house really
won't really eat it,

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:49.941
'cause there's caraway
seeds in there,

00:06:49.941 --> 00:06:55.481
and it's really kind of
baking soda-y and baking --

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:58.251
it's just a lot of flour,
and it's -- I love it.

00:06:58.251 --> 00:07:00.186
I think it's great.
Irish people love it.

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:02.387
But, again, if you make this
at home,

00:07:02.387 --> 00:07:03.989
you'll be the only
one kind of eating it.

00:07:03.989 --> 00:07:06.559
I mean, honey, you can have
a piece if you'd like.

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:08.094
-I'm good, thanks.
-Yeah, I know.

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:12.698
But if you're gonna do it,
use Kerrygold butter.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:15.033
This is like --
the Irish butter is the best,

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:16.468
and you put that on there.

00:07:16.468 --> 00:07:19.172
It's really thick, kind of
yellow-y type of butter.

00:07:19.172 --> 00:07:23.376
And...

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:25.311
Cheers! Is that disgusting?

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:27.546
-[ Chuckles ]

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:31.483
-That's good.

00:07:31.483 --> 00:07:33.786
Are you zooming in?
What are you doing?

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:37.289
-[ Chuckles ]

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:40.058
-Well...

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:42.394
I -- Thank you.

00:07:42.394 --> 00:07:46.532
It's very dry.

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:50.669
Okay.
It's really, really good.

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:52.538
Happy St. Patrick's Day
to everybody.

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:54.373
Okay, guys.
That's our little show.

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:57.543
Again, if you can donate
to feedingamerica.org,

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:58.911
that would be really helpful.

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:01.013
Thank you to Winnie Fallon
for drawing these up for me

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:04.016
and Franny Fallon for not
participating in the show --

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:06.986
Well, a little musical
accompaniment at the beginning.

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:08.787
And of course, I want to
thank my wife, Nancy.

00:08:08.787 --> 00:08:09.988
You are awesome, buddy.

00:08:09.988 --> 00:08:13.192
I figured let's end this
with a little song,

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.327
and since it's
St. Patrick's Day,

00:08:15.327 --> 00:08:20.733
this one's called
"St. Patrick's Day Quarantine."

00:08:24.169 --> 00:08:29.475 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:32.578
♪ Well, it's St. Paddy's Day,
I'm quarantined ♪

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.847
♪ I'm in me house alone ♪

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:36.816
♪ No one to drink
a Guinness with ♪

00:08:36.816 --> 00:08:38.918
♪ Unless it's through me phone ♪

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:43.255
♪ So kiss me, I'm Irish,
but stay six feet away ♪

00:08:43.255 --> 00:08:47.426
♪ 'Cause no one wants to get
a virus on St. Paddy's Day ♪

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:50.496 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:54.566
♪ I'm socially distancing
and stocking up on cans ♪

00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:58.771
♪ With four-leaf clovers on
my mind and Purell on my hands ♪

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:00.773
♪ And if you try
to shake my hands ♪

00:09:00.773 --> 00:09:02.808
♪ I'll kick ya in the rump ♪

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:05.010
♪ So do not kiss
the Blarney Stone ♪

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:07.612
♪ Just give it an elbow bump ♪

00:09:07.612 --> 00:09:10.282
Happy St. Patrick's Day,
everybody!

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:11.783
Ye-hoo!

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:15.087
Uh, all right, guys.
I'm gonna go.

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:17.956
Please watch the rest
of our show on NBC.

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:22.561
We are putting our best reruns
we can on there for you.

00:09:22.561 --> 00:09:25.297
We do want to entertain you.
This is tough times.

00:09:25.297 --> 00:09:27.733
We can get through
this together.

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:29.134
We can.

00:09:29.134 --> 00:09:30.803
Be safe.

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.271
Wash your hands.

00:09:32.271 --> 00:09:34.773
And don't touch your face!

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:35.875
See you tomorrow!

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:37.877
Wheee!

